    "title": "Article 153: Governors of States",
    "definition": "There shall be a Governor for each State. Provided that nothing in this article shall prevent the appointment of the same person as Governor for two or more States.",
    "explanation": "Each State shall have a Governor. One person can be Governor of two or more States (7th Amendment). The Governor is the constitutional head of the State.",
