      "**Governor's Pardon:** State Governors regularly exercise pardon power for state law offences.",
      "**Raj Bhavan:** Each state's Governor resides at the Raj Bhavan (Governor's House).",
      "**Age Qualification:** Governors must be 35+ years and Indian citizens — same as the President.",
      "**Oath Before CJ:** The Governor takes oath before the Chief Justice of the state's High Court.",
      "**Resignation:** Governors resign by writing to the President — several have resigned for political reasons.",
      "**Acting Governor:** When the Governor's office is vacant, the Chief Justice of the HC may be asked to discharge functions."
