      "**Rajasthan Assembly:** 200 members — one of the larger unicameral legislatures.",
      "**Governor's Address:** Each state legislative year begins with the Governor's address — debated as Motion of Thanks.",
      "**Speaker of Assembly:** The Speaker of the Legislative Assembly presides, decides anti-defection cases.",
      "**Chairman of Council:** The Legislative Council's Chairman presides over Council proceedings.",
      "**Sessions:** State legislatures typically meet in Budget and other sessions — at least twice a year.",
      "**Assembly Dissolution:** Governors have dissolved Assemblies — some controversially (Arunachal Pradesh 2016).",
      "**Teachers' Constituency:** Legislative Council members elected by teachers form a unique constituency.",
      "**Graduates' Constituency:** Graduates of three years' standing elect Council members.",
      "**Governor's Nominations:** Governor nominates distinguished persons to the Legislative Council."
